ested_fix":"Split compound criteria, replace subjective terms with observable outcomes, and state how each is verified.","tier":"DET","validity":1.0,"verification":null},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Reuse rebar.llm.structured's deterministic object-recovery (`_first_json_object`/`tolerant_parse`) for the digest JSON/prose step instead of embedding.py's `_first_balanced_object`, or state in the plan why the digest path cannot use the existing authority (import-purity, 4-field semantics, YAML tier) and why a first-balance-without-parse scan is acceptable.","cohort":["A1"],"criteria":["A1"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.95,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["structured.py:258 docstring: 'Order (all NO-LLM): strict json.loads -> fenced block -> the FIRST balanced {...} object (deterministic, first-wins on multi-object / prose-wrapped)'","structured.py:216-252 `_first_json_object` tracks string literals and ADVANCES to the next '{' when a region fails to parse (bug 67ee: a `${{ }}` preamble no longer aborts the scan)","embedding.py:175-205 `_first_balanced_object` returns the first brace-balanced substring WITHOUT checking it parses as JSON, then embedding.py:261-266 tries json.loads on only that one span — so a non-JSON balanced preamble silently loses the trailing real object, the exact failure 67ee fixed","Plan 'Digest step' specifies 'extract the first balanced object embedded in the text' with no mention of the existing structured authority or why it is not reused"],"finding":"The digest reply-recovery ladder (strict JSON -> first balanced object in prose, string-aware brace tracking) duplicates the existing deterministic authority in rebar.llm.structured rather than reusing it, and the bespoke copy is weaker than the original.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f23aa7092b507f466","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Plan section 'Digest step'; src/rebar/similar/embedding.py `_first_balanced_object`/`recover_digest` (175-273) vs src/rebar/llm/structured.py `_first_json_object`/`tolerant_parse` (216-259)","norm_id":"nc1a2b63f4785669f","priority":0.0,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A model emits a prose preamble containing a `{...}` fragment (e.g. a templated expression or an example) before the real digest JSON: structured's parser recovers the digest; embedding.py's picks the preamble span, fails json.loads, and counts the reply as digest_unparsed -> needless retry / eventual digest_failed and degradation"],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Have `recover_digest` call `rebar.llm.structured._first_json_object` (or `tolerant_parse`) for the JSON/embedded-object tiers, keeping only the digest-specific YAML tier and `_unwrap`/4-field logic local; if structured's import footprint is the blocker, note that the build path already loads the agent stack.","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"no","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"no","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] State the vector index's write ownership/serialization (concurrent builds, build-vs-query) and whether key-invalidated/orphaned vectors are retired or left to accumulate.","cohort":["E3","E5","G5","T5b","T6","T9","necessity","project.failure-disposition-contract","project.portability"],"criteria":["T9"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.884,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["'a separate explicit build_vectors(tracker) in embedding.py that a caller invokes' — no ownership/locking stated for concurrent invocation","'changing either invalidates those entries' / AC5-AC6 'assert they re-embed' — invalidation re-embeds, but no RETIRE path is stated for vectors in a now-dead embedding space that are never re-embedded (e.g. a ticket deleted or permanently unvectored)","Validity-key gating tolerates staleness at read time, but write-time concurrency (two builds, or build vs. the inline create-path reader) is unspecified"],"finding":"The vector index is new shared state keyed by a validity key, but the plan does not state who owns the index write during a build nor how concurrent builds (or a build racing a query) are serialized; it also does not state whether key-invalidated vectors are removed/retired or merely ignored, so stale-space entries could accumulate across repeated key changes.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f498ce87dc9c857c4","impact":0.264,"is_primary":null,"location":"Constraints: 'The build is a separate explicit build_vectors(tracker)...'; 'Cosine ranking requires full current-key coverage'","norm_id":"nd9cac49f654a77d4","priority":0.066,"reason":"veto:absence-refuted","recalled":false,"scenarios":[],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.25,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"no","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"no","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"low"}}},{"block_threshold":0.9,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] State, per degrade arm (timeout/denial vs missing-backend vs digest-unparsed), the disposition surfaced using an explicit retryable/transient-vs-fatal word, and that the diagnostic preserves the most-recoverable leg rather than flattening all arms to one exit-0 degrade.","cohort":["E3","E5","G5","T5b","T6","T9","necessity","project.failure-disposition-contract","project.portability"],"criteria":["project.failure-disposition-contract"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.9,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["'Degrade means retrieval returns the lexical tier's whole-corpus results, the create advisory carries them, a diagnostic is emitted and create exits 0.' — one disposition for all arms","AC11 (missing backend / ImportError) and AC12 (denial or timeout) both reduce to the same 'degrade' outcome with no retryable/fatal distinction","Criterion's 1c0d pattern: the diagnostic should preserve the most-recoverable leg's disposition (a retryable Bedrock 429 vs a permanent missing-group ImportError) rather than flattening both to exit-0"],"finding":"The embedding tier adds a fallback arm (degrade to lexical) covering distinct failure modes — provider denial, timeout, missing optional backend, all-empty/unparsed digest — but the plan collapses all of them into one uniform terminal 'degrade + exit 0' disposition without an explicit disposition word (retryable/transient vs fatal/permanent). A timeout or provider throttle (retryable) is surfaced identically to a permanent missing-backend ImportError (fatal), so the retryable leg's disposition is not preserved or communicated at degrade time.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f000aa25b0b1f3241","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Constraints: 'Degrade means retrieval returns the lexical tier's whole-corpus results...'; AC12 'A provider denial or timeout degrades'","norm_id":"n115aecf33201dac6","priority":0.0,"reason":"veto:absence-refuted","recalled":false,"scenarios":[],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.375,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"no","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.8,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] State in the plan that the query is digested through the SAME pinned-prompt digest path as the corpus (symmetric `vector`), and add an AC asserting the query traverses the digest step (not raw-text embedding), so the shipped tier matches ADR 0122's measured candidate.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.7022,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan 'Digest step' describes digesting only in the build context ('one LLM call plus one embed per ticket'); it never says the QUERY is digested.","AC1 asserts only 'retrieval cosine-ranks the vectors ... assert the ordering' — satisfiable by embedding raw query text, which produces a valid ordering but not ADR 0122's measured recall.","docs/adr/0122: `vector-raw` (Titan v2 over raw title+description) scores semantic recall@5 0.839 vs `vector`'s 0.876; the measured win belongs to the digest-embedded path on BOTH sides.","src/rebar/similar/embedding.py docstring: 'Embedding raw query text against a digest-embedded corpus is neither `vector` nor the rejected `vector-raw` diagnostic but an unmeasured hybrid ... would make the tier's whole justification inapplicable'; `_embed_query` calls `_paragraph_for` to digest the query."],"finding":"The plan never states that the query must itself be digested before embedding — yet ADR 0122's adopted `vector` candidate is symmetric (query and corpus vectors are both embeddings of the LLM digest paragraph), so embedding raw query text against a digest-embedded corpus is the unmeasured `vector`/`vector-raw` hybrid that carries none of the measured recall@5=0.876 the whole tier is justified by.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f8de02e323be18164","impact":0.44,"is_primary":null,"location":"Plan sections 'Digest step' and 'Acceptance Criteria' (AC1: 'A provider:model string resolves via infer_embedding_model and retrieval cosine-ranks the vectors').","norm_id":"n1128c5e99afb3c26","priority":0.0978,"reason":"veto:absence-refuted","recalled":false,"scenarios":["An implementer reads the plan, embeds the raw query title+description against the digest-embedded corpus, and passes AC1 (ordering holds) — shipping a tier whose recall is the unmeasured hybrid, not the 0.876 the tier exists to deliver."],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"In 'Digest step' add that ranking digests the query with the same pinned prompt before embedding (per ADR 0122's symmetric `vector`), and amend AC1 (or add an AC) to assert the query is digest-embedded — e.g. that the digest model is invoked once per query and raw-text query embedding is rejected.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.2222,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"no","asserted_capability_confirmed":"no","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"yes","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"no","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"underspecified_oracle","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"none","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.9,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Add `src/rebar/_config_sections.py` (`_LLM_KNOWN_KEYS`) to the edit set, inserting `embedding_model` and `similar_digest_model` so the drift test `tests/unit/test_config_llm_known_keys.py` passes and the keys are not warned as unknown.","cohort":["project.symbol-reference-completeness"],"criteria":["project.symbol-reference-completeness"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.9,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan: 'The edit set the two keys require. `llm/config.py` declares the fields; `llm/config_readers.py` resolves them via `_llm_str` ... `docs/env-vars.md` is GENERATED ... `tests/golden/config_surface.json` is NOT touched' — enumerates config.py, config_readers.py, env-vars.md, census markers, but not _config_sections.py.","src/rebar/_config_sections.py:216 `_LLM_KNOWN_KEYS: tuple[str